"hadiths[277]{hadithnumber,text}:"
991,"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, ""Read the Qur'an, for it will come as an intercessor for its reciters on the Day of Resurrection."" [Muslim] ."
992,"On the authority of Al-Nawwas bin Samaan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “On the Day of Resurrection, the Qur’an will be brought and its people who used to act upon it in this world will be preceded by Surat Al-Baqarah and Al Imran, arguing on behalf of their companion” [Muslim]."
993,"- On the authority of Othman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best of you is the one who learns and teaches the Qur’an” [Al-Bukhari]."
994,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The one who is proficient in the recitation of the Qur'an will be with the honourable and obedient scribes (angels) and he who recites the Qur'an and finds it difficult to recite, doing his best to recite it in the best way possible, will have two rewards."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
995,"On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The example of a believing man who recites the Qur'an is like a citron: its fragrance is pleasant and its taste is good. The example of a believing man who does not recite the Qur'an is like a date: it has no fragrance and its taste is sweet. The example of a hypocrite who recites the Qur'an is like basil: its fragrance is pleasant and its taste is bitter. The example of a hypocrite who does not recite the Qur'an is like colocynth: it has no fragrance and its taste is bitter.” (Agreed upon)"
996,"On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Allah raises people with this book and lowers others with it” [Muslim]."
997,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both: On the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “There is no envy except in two things: a man to whom Allah has given the Qur’an, and he recites it throughout the night and during the day, and a man to whom Allah has given money, so he spends it throughout the night and during the day.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. (1)."
998,"On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: A man was reciting Surah Al-Kahf, and he had a horse tied with two saddle straps. Then a cloud covered it and it began to approach, and it caused his horse to shy away from it. When the morning came, he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him, and he said: “That is tranquility revealed for the Qur’an” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
999,"On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever recites a letter from the Book of Allah will have a good deed, and a good deed is multiplied ten times as much. I do not say that Alif-Lam-Mim is one letter, but [I say that] Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter” [Al-Tirmidhi narrated it and said: A good and authentic hadith]."
1000,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""He who does not memorize any part from the Qur'an he is like the ruined house.'' [At-Tirmidhi] ."
1001,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “It will be said to the reciter of the Qur’an: Read, ascend, and recite as you used to recite in this world, for your status is at the last verse you recite.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
1002,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Read the Qur'an regularly. By the One in Whose Hand Muhammad's soul is, it escapes from memory faster than a camel does from its tying ropes."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1003,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The parable of one who knows the Qur'an by heart is as the parable of an owner of hobbled camel. If he remains vigilant, he will retain it; and if he neglects it, it will go away."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1004,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Allah did not permit anything. He permitted a prophet with a beautiful voice to sing the Qur’an and recite it aloud.” (Agreed upon)"
1005,"On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: “I have come to you with a melodious voice like the psalms of the family of David” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: “If you had seen me listening to your reading yesterday.”"
1006,"I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) reciting Surat Wat-Teen Waz-Zaitun (Chapter 95) during the 'Isha' prayer. I have never heard anyone reciting it in a more beautiful voice than his. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1007,"On the authority of Abu Lubabah Bashir bin Abdul-Mundhir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever does not sing the Qur’an is not one of us.” [Abu Dawud]."
1008,"On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: “Recite the Qur’an to me.” So I said: O Messenger of Allah, should I recite the Quran to you, when it was revealed to you?! He said: “I would love to hear it from others.” So I recited Surah An-Nisa to him until I came to this verse: {So how if We bring from every nation a witness? And We have brought you as a witness over these people. He said: “It suffices for you now.” He turned to him, and saw his eyes streaming with tears. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1009,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Rafi’ bin Al-Mu’alla, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “Shall I not teach you the greatest surah in the Qur’an before you leave the mosque?” So he took my hand, and when we wanted to leave, I said: O Messenger of Allah, you said, “Should I teach you the greatest surah in the Qur’an?” He said: “Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds, and it is the seven repeated verses, and the Great Qur'an that you have been given.” [Al-Bukhari]."
1010,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said in: {Say: He is Allah, One}: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” And in a narration: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to his companions: “Is any of you unable to recite a third of the Qur’an in a night?” This made them distressed, and they said: Who can bear that, O Messenger? Allah: So he said: “{Say: He is Allah, One.} One-third of the Qur’an.” [Al-Bukhari]."
1011,"A man heard another reciting Surat Al-Ikhlas repeatedly. The next morning he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and informed him about it. On that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, this Surah is equal to one-third of the Qur'an."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
1012,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about: {Say: He is Allah, One} “It is equivalent to a third of the Qur’an.” [Muslim]."
1013,"A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I love Surat-Al-Ikhlas [Say: He is Allah, (the) One] ."" He (ﷺ) said, ""Your love for it will admit you to Jannah."" [At-Tirmidhi] ."
1014,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do you not know that last night certain Ayat were revealed the like of which there is no precedence. They are: 'Say: I seek refuge with (Allah) the Rubb of the daybreak' (Surah 113), and 'Say: I seek refuge with (Allah) the Rubb of mankind' (Surah 114)."" [Muslim] ."
1015,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was seeking refuge from the jinn and the evil eye of man, until the two refuges were revealed, and when they were revealed, he took them and left everything else. [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1016,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""There is a Surah in the Qur'an which contains thirty Ayat which kept interceding for a man until his sins are forgiven. This Surah is 'Blessed is He in Whose Hand is the dominion.' (Surat Al-Mulk 67)."" [At-Tirmidhi and Abu Dawud] ."
1017,"On the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Badri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surat Al-Baqarah in a night, it is sufficient for him” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1018,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Do not make your homes graves, for Satan flees from the house in which Surat Al-Baqarah is recited” [Muslim]."
1019,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Abu Mundhir! Do you know which Ayah in Allah's Book is the greatest?"" I replied: ""It is 'Allah la ilaha illa Huwal-Haiyul-Qayum (Allah! none has the right to be worshipped but He, the Ever Living...)'."" (2:256) Thereupon he (ﷺ) patted me in the chest and said, ""Rejoice by this knowledge, O Abu Mundhir!"" [Muslim] ."
1020,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entrusted me with preserving the zakat of Ramadan. A man came to me and began to eat some food. I took it and said: I will take you to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: I am in need, I have children, and I am in dire need. So I left him, and in the morning the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Abu Hurairah, what did your prisoner do yesterday? “I said: O Messenger of Allah, he complained of need and family, so I had mercy on him, so I let him go. He said: “But he has lied to you and will return.” I knew that he would return to what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, so I tracked him down. He came seeking food, so I said: I will take you to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: Let me. For I am in need, and I have dependents, I will not return, so I had mercy on him and let him go. In the morning, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: “O Abu Hurairah, what did your prisoner do yesterday?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, he complained of need and dependents, so I had mercy on him, so I let him go. He said: “He has lied to you and will return.” So I tracked him for the third time. So he came in search of food. So I took it and said: I will take you to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and this is the last of the three that you claim that you will not return, and then you return! He said: Let me teach you words that Allah will benefit you with. I said: What are they? He said: If you go to bed, recite Ayat al-Kursi, for there will never cease to be a guardian from Allah, and no devil will approach you until morning. So I let him go, and the morning came, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me. He said to me: “What did your prisoner do yesterday?” I said: O Messenger of Allah, he claimed that he was teaching me words that Allah would benefit me with, so I let him go. He said: “What are they?” I said: He said to me: If you go to bed, recite Ayat al-Kursi from the beginning until the verse ends: {Allah, there is no god but He, the Ever-Living, the Ever-Subsisting} And he said to me: You still have a guardian from Allah, and no devil will approach you until morning. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “But he has told you the truth while he is a liar. You have learned who you have been talking to for three days, O Abu Hurairah.” I said: No. He said: “That is Satan.” [Al-Bukhari]."
1021,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever commits to memory the first ten Ayat of the Surat Al-Kahf, will be protected from (the trial of) Ad-Dajjal (Antichrist)."" [Muslim] . In another narration, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""(Whoever commits to memory) the last ten Ayat of Surat Al-Kahf, he will be protected from (the trial of) Ad-Dajjal (Antichrist)."""
1022,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: While Gabriel, (ﷺ) was sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) he heard something from above him, so he raised his head and said: “This is a door from heaven that was opened today and has never been opened except today. Then an angel descended from it and said: This is an angel who descended to earth and has never descended except today. So he greeted and said: Good news of two lights that you have been given that were not given to a prophet before you: the opening of the Book, and the endings of Surah Al-Baqarah, you will not recite a letter from them without being granted a reward for it.” [Muslim]. The opposite: the sound."
1023,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No people gather in a house of Allah’s houses, reciting the Book of Allah, and studying it among themselves, except that tranquility descends upon them, mercy envelops them, angels surround them, and Allah remembers them among those with Him” [Muslim]."
1024,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “On the Day of Resurrection, my nation will be summoned with white faces and limbs bearing the traces of ablution. So whoever of you is able to extend his white mark (of ablution), let him do so” (Agreed upon)."
1025,"On his authority, he said: I heard my friend (ﷺ) say: “The believer’s adornment reaches the point where ablution is attained” [Muslim]."
1026,"On the authority of Othman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution and does it well, his sins will leave his body until they come out from under his fingernails” [Muslim]."
1027,"On his authority, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performing ablution like this one of mine. Then he said: “Whoever performs ablution like this, his previous sins will be forgiven, and his prayer and walking to the mosque will be voluntary” [Muslim]."
1028,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a Muslim servant - or a believer - performs ablution and washes his face, every sin that he saw with his eyes will come out of his face with the water, or with the last drop of water. And if he washes his hands, every sin that his hands committed will come out of his hands with the water, or with the last drop of water. If he washes his feet, every sin that his feet committed will come out with the water, or with the last drop of water, until he comes out pure from Sins” [Muslim]."
1029,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went to the (Baqi') cemetery and said, ""May you be secured from punishment, O dwellers of abode of the believers! We, if Allah wills, will follow you. I wish we see my brothers."" The Companions said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Are not we your brothers?"" He (ﷺ) said, ""You are my Companions, but my brothers are those who have not come into the world yet."" They said; ""O Messenger of Allah! How will you recognize those of your Ummah who are not born yet?"" He (ﷺ) said, ""Say, if a man has white-footed horses with white foreheads among horses which are pure black, will he not recognize his own horses?"" They said; ""Certainly, O Messenger of Allah!"" He (ﷺ) said, ""They (my followers) will come with bright faces and white limbs because of Wudu'; and I will arrive at the Haud (Al-Kauthar) ahead of them."" [Muslim] ."
1030,"Abu Hurairah (May Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Shall I not tell you something by which Allah effaces the sins and elevates ranks (in Jannah)?"" The Companions said; ""Certainly, O Messenger of Allah."" He (ﷺ) said, ""Performing the Wudu' thoroughly in spite of difficult circumstances, walking with more paces to the mosque, and waiting for the next As- Salat (the prayer) after observing Salat; and that is Ar-Ribat, and that is Ar-Ribat."" [Muslim] ."
1031,"On the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Purity is half of faith” [Muslim]. It was previously mentioned at length in the chapter on patience. In the chapter is the hadith of Amr bin Absa, may Allah be pleased with him, which was mentioned earlier at the end of the chapter on hope, and it is a great hadith, containing a number of good deeds."
1032,"On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “None of you performs ablution and completes the ablution - or completes the ablution - and then says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His slave and Messenger, except that the eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him and he may enter through whichever one he wishes” [Muslim]. Al-Tirmidhi added: “O Allah, make me one of those who repent and make me one of those who purify themselves.”"
1033,"- On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If people knew what is in the call and the first row and then had no choice but to draw arrows for it, they would have drawn arrows for it, and if they knew what is in coming early to prayer, they would have rushed to it, and if they knew what is in the dark and the morning, they would have come even if they had crawled.” (Agreed upon)). Al-Hajjar: arriving early to prayer"
1034,"On the authority of Muawiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “The muezzins will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection” [Muslim]."
1035,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Sa’sa’a, that Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: “I see that you love sheep and the desert. If you are among your sheep - or your desert - and you call for prayer, raise your voice with the call, for no jinn, human, or any creature can hear the full voice of the muezzin, except that all who hear it will bear witness for him on the Day of Resurrection.” Abu Saeed said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Al-Bukhari]."
1036,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When the call to prayer is called, Satan turns away, his farts so that he does not hear the call to prayer, and when the call is finished, he comes forward, until the iqama is called for prayer, he turns away. And when the iqama is finished, he comes close, until he comes between a person and his own thoughts, saying: Remember such-and-such, and remember such-and-such - that which was not mentioned before - until the man remains in prayer, not knowing how many rak'ahs he has prayed."
1037,"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, ""When you hear the Adhan, repeat what the Mu'adhdhin says. Then ask Allah to exalt my mention because everyone who does so will receive in return ten rewards from Allah. Then beseech Allah to grant me Al-Wasilah, which is a high rank in Jannah, fitting for only one of Allah's slaves; and I hope that I will be that man. If any one asks Al-Wasilah for me, it becomes incumbent upon me to intercede for him."" [Muslim]"
1038,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When you hear the Mu'adhdhin (pronouncing the call to Salat), repeat after him what he says."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1039,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""He who says upon hearing the Adhan: 'Allahumma Rabba hadhihid-da'wati-ttammati, was-salatil-qa'imati, ati Muhammadanil-wasilata wal-fadhilata, wab'athu maqaman mahmuda nilladhi wa 'adtahu [O Allah, Rubb of this perfect call (Da'wah) and of the established prayer (As-Salat), grant Muhammad the Wasilah and superiority, and raise him up to a praiseworthy position which You have promised him] ', it becomes incumbent upon me to intercede for him on the Day of Resurrection."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
1040,"On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: “Whoever says when he hears the muezzin: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, I am satisfied with Allah as my Lord and with Islam as our religion, his sin will be forgiven” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1041,"On the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: “A supplication is not rejected between the call to prayer and the iqama.” [Abu Dawud]"
1042,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Do you think that if there was a river at the door of one of you and he bathed in it five times every day, would any dirt remain on him?” They said: Nothing of dirt would remain on him. He said: “That is like the five daily prayers, and through them Allah erases sins.” (Agreed upon) On him).."
1043,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The example of the five prayers is like a deep river flowing at the door of one of you, from which he bathes five times every day.” [Muslim]."
1044,"A man kissed a woman. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and informed him about it. Then Allah revealed this Ayah: ""And perform the Salat, between the two ends of the day and in some hours of the night. Verily, the good deeds efface the evil deeds (i.e., minor sins)."" (11:114) The man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) whether this applies to him only. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""It applies to all of my Ummah."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1045,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The five (daily) Salat (prayers) and the Friday (prayer) to the Friday (prayer) expiate whatever (minor sins) may be committed in between, so long as major sins are avoided."" [Muslim] ."
1046,"On the authority of Othman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: “There is no Muslim who attends an prescribed prayer and performs its ablution, humility, and bowing well except that it is an expiation for the sins that preceded it, unless major ones were committed, and that is for an entire eternity” [Muslim]."
1047,"On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prays Al-Bardain will enter Paradise” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1048,"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ""He who performs Salat (prayers) before the rising of the sun and before its setting, will not enter the Hell."" [Muslim] ."
1049,"On the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prays the Fajr prayer is under Allah’s protection, so look, son of Adam. Allah will not ask you for anything from His protection.” [Muslim]."
1050,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Angels succeed one another among you at night, and angels during the day, and they gather for the morning prayer and the afternoon prayer. Then those who spent the night among you ascend, and Allah - and He knows best about them - asks them: How did you leave My servants? They say: We left them while they were praying, and we came to them while they were praying.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1051,"- On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: “You will see your Lord as you see this moon, and you will see Him clearly without any obstruction. If you are able not to neglect a prayer before the sun rises and before it sets, then do so” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. ((And in Narration: “So he looked at the moon on the night of the fourteenth.”).."
1052,"On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever neglects the afternoon prayer, his work has been nullified” [Al-Bukhari]."
1053,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever goes to the mosque or comes, Allah will prepare for him a dwelling in Paradise each time he goes or comes.” (Agreed upon)."
1054,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""He who purifies (performs Wudu') himself in his house and then walks to one of the houses of Allah (mosque) for performing an obligatory Salat, one step of his will wipe out his sins and another step will elevate his rank (in Jannah)."" [Muslim] ."
1055,"On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There was a man from the Ansar, and I do not know of anyone farther from the mosque than him, and his prayer was not missed! He was told: If you bought a donkey, you would ride it in the dark and in the rain. He said: I would not be happy if my house was next to the mosque. I want my walk to the mosque and my return to be recorded for me when I return to my family. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Allah has gathered.” All of that is yours.” [Muslim]."
1056,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The areas around the mosque were deserted, so Banu Salama wanted to move near the mosque. This was reported to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said to them: “I have heard that you want to move near the mosque? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we wanted that. He said: ‘Bani Salamah, your homes write your traces, your homes write your traces.’ They said: It would not be better for us if we had moved away from our homes.” [Narrated by Muslim, and Al-Bukhari narrated its meaning from the narration of Anas]."
1057,"On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The person with the greatest reward for prayer is the one who walks the furthest to it, so the furthest away, and the one who waits for the prayer until he prays it with the imam is of greater reward than the one who prays it and then sleeps” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1058,"On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ): “Give good news to those who walk in darkness to the mosques; they will be granted complete light on the Day of Resurrection on the Day of Resurrection” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
1059,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Shall I not tell you something by which Allah effaces the sins and elevates the ranks (in Jannah)."" The Companions said: ""Yes (please tell us), O Messenger of Allah."" He said, ""Performing the Wudu' properly in spite of difficult circumstances, walking with more paces to the mosque, and waiting for the next Salat (prayer) after a observing Salat; and that is Ar-Ribat, and that is Ar-Ribat."" [Muslim] ."
1060,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If you see a man accustomed to the mosques, bear witness to his faith. Allah Almighty said: ‘The mosques of Allah are inhabited only by those who believe in Allah and the Last Day’ [The verse. It was narrated by Al-Tirmidhi and he said it is a good hadith]."
1061,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “One of you continues to pray as long as the prayer detains him. Nothing prevents him from returning to his family except prayer” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1062,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The angels supplicate in favour of one of you so long as he remains in the place where he has performed Salat (prayer), unless he breaks ritual purity (hadath). They (the angels) say: 'O Allah! Forgive him, O Allah! Have mercy on him.""' [Al- Bukhari] ."
1063,"Once the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delayed the night prayer ('Isha') till midnight. He (ﷺ) turned to us after Salat (prayer) and said, ""The people slept after performing their Salat, but you who waited, will be accounted as engaged in Salat throughout the period of your waiting."" [Al-Bukhari] ."
1064,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Salat in congregation is twenty-seven times more meritorious than a Salat performed individually."" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1065,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “A man’s prayer in congregation is twenty-five times greater than his prayer in his home and in the market, and that is because if he performs ablution and performs it well, then goes out to the mosque, and nothing takes him out except for prayer, he does not take a step without his being raised in rank and a sin removed from him because of it, so if he prays the angels do not cease praying over him as long as he is in his place of prayer, unless he breaks ritual purity. They (the angels) say: ‘O Allah, bless him, O Allah, have mercy on him.’ And he continues to pray as long as he waits for the prayer.” (Agreed upon. This is Al-Bukhari’s wording))"
1066,"On his authority, he said: A blind man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not have a guide to lead me to the mosque. So he asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to give him permission to pray in his house, so he granted him permission. When he left, he called him and said to him: “Do you hear the call to prayer?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then answer” (Narrated by: Muslim).."
1067,"And on the authority of Abdullah - and it was said: Amr bin Qais, known as Ibn Umm Maktoum, the muezzin, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, the city is full of vermin and predators. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You hear, ‘Come to the prayer, come to the farmer, come to the farmer,’ so welcome.” [Narrated by Abu Dawud with a good chain of transmission. (12]"
1068,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I was about to order firewood and it would be gathered, then I would order the prayer and the call to prayer would be given to it, then I would order a man and he would lead the people in prayer, then I would go to other men and burn their houses over them” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1069,"On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whoever is pleased to meet Allah Almighty tomorrow in peace, let him observe these prayers wherever he calls them, for Allah has prescribed for your Prophet (ﷺ) the Sunnahs of guidance, and they are Sunnahs of guidance. If you had prayed in your homes as this person who lags behind in attending the congregation prays in his house, you would have abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, and if you had abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, you would have gone astray. We have seen that none abandon them except a known hypocrite. And a man would be brought to him, guided between two men until he was made to stand in the row. [Narrated by Muslim, and in his narration he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught us the ways of guidance, and among the guidance is prayer in the mosque in which the call to prayer is given]."
1070,"On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “There are not three people in a village or nomad among whom prayer is not performed except that Satan has taken control of them. So you must adhere to the congregation, for the wolf only eats from the far-away sheep” [Abu Dawud]."
1071,"On the authority of Othman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “Whoever prays Isha’ in a group, it is as if he has risen at midnight, and whoever prays Fajr in a group, it is as if he prayed the whole night.” [Muslim]. And in the narration of Al-Tirmidhi on the authority of Othman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever witnesses the evening prayer in a group will have a night’s prayer for him, and whoever witnesses the evening prayer and dawn prayer in a group, his prayer will be as if he has spent a night in prayer.” [Al-Tirmidhi said, a good and authentic hadith]"
1072,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If they knew what is in the dark and the morning, they would have entered into it even if they had crawled” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. It has been mentioned previously."
1073,"On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “There is no prayer heavier for the hypocrites than the Fajr and Isha prayers, and if they knew what is in them, they would have performed them even if they had crawled” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1074,"On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): Which deeds are best? He said: “Prayer at its appointed time.” I said: “Then what?” He said: “Honoring one’s parents.” I said: “Then what?” He said: “Jihad for the sake of Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1075,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Islam is built on five things: bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, paying zakat, performing the Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1076,"On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “I have been commanded to fight the people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and perform prayer and pay zakat. If they do that, their blood and their wealth will be protected from me except for the right of Islam, and their reckoning will be with Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1077,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me as a governor to Yemen and (at the time of departure) he instructed me thus: ""You will go to people of the Scripture (i.e., the Jews and the Christians). First of all invite them to testify that La ilaha ill Allah (There is no true god except Allah) and that Muhammad (ﷺ) is the Messenger of Allah; and if they accept this, then tell them that Allah has enjoined upon them five Salat (prayers) during the day and night; and if they accept it, then tell them that Allah has made the payment of Zakat obligatory upon them. It should be collected from their rich and distributed among their poor; and if they agree to it, beware of the best of their wealth. Beware of the supplications of the oppressed, for there is no barrier between it and Allah."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1078,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Between a man and disbelief and paganism is the abandonment of Salat (prayer)."" [Muslim] ."
1079,"On the authority of Buraydah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The covenant between us and them is prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1080,"And on the authority of Shaqiq bin Abdullah al-Tabi’i, whose eminence is unanimously recognized, may Allah have mercy on him, he said: The companions of Muhammad (ﷺ) did not consider any of the deeds left as disbelief other than prayer. [Narrated by al-Tirmidhi in the Book of Faith with an authentic chain of transmission]."
1081,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The first thing for which a servant will be held accountable on the Day of Resurrection regarding his work is his prayer. If it is righteous, he has succeeded and prospered, and if it is corrupted, then he has failed and lost. If he diminished anything from his obligatory prayer, the Lord, Almighty and Majestic, said: See if my servant has voluntary prayers, so that I may complete from them what he missed of the obligatory prayer Then the rest of his deeds will be judged in this same manner” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1082,"On the authority of Jabir bin Samra, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came out to us and said: “Don’t you line up as the angels line up before their Lord?” So we said: O Messenger of Allah, and how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: “They complete the first rows, and line up in line.” [Muslim].."
1083,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""If people came to know the blessing of calling Adhan and the standing in the first row, they could do nothing but would draw lots to secure these privileges."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1084,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The best of the men's rows (in Salat) is the first row and the worst is the last; but the best of the woman's row is the last and the worst of their rows is the first."" [Muslim] ."
1085,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw that his companions were late, so he said to them: “Go ahead and follow me, and let those after you come with you. A people will continue to delay until Allah delays them” [Muslim]."
1086,"On the authority of Abu Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to wipe our shoulders during prayer, and say: “Stay equal and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Those of maturity and sound judgment among you will be closest to me, then those after them, then those after them.” [Muslim]."
1087,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Straighten your rows, for straightening the row is part of completing the prayer.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] And in Al-Bukhari’s narration: “For straightening the rows is part of establishing the prayer.”"
1088,"On his authority, he said: The prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned to us with his face and said: “Strengthen your rows and close together, for I see you behind my back” [Narrated by Al-Bukhari with his wording, and Muslim with his meaning]. And in a narration by Al-Bukhari: And one of us was pressing his shoulder against his companion’s shoulder and his foot with his foot.”"
1089,"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying, ""Straighten your rows; otherwise, Allah will create dissension among you."" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] . The narration in Muslim is: An-Nu'man bin Bashir (May Allah be pleased with them) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) directed us to keep our rows as straight as arrows. He continued stressing this until he realized that we had learnt it from him (recognized its significance). One day he went out and stood up. He was just about to say Takbir (Allah is Greater) when he noticed a man whose chest was projected from the row, so he said, ""O slaves of Allah, you must straighten your rows or Allah will certainly put your faces in opposite directions."""
1090,"On the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to move from one side to the other, stroking our chests and shoulders and saying: “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ.” And he used to say: “Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first rows” [Abu Dawud]."
1091,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Straighten rows, keep your shoulders aligned, fill gaps, be gentle with your brothers using your hands, and do not leave any openings for Satan. Whoever joins a line, Allah will connect him, and whoever breaks a line, Allah will cut him off.” [Abu Dawud]."
1092,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Align your rows, close together and align your necks, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I see Satan entering through a gap in the row, as if it were a deletion” [An authentic hadith narrated by Abu Dawud with a chain of transmission according to Muslim’s condition]."
1093,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Fill (complete) the first row, then the one next to it; and if there is any deficiency (incompleteness), it should be in the last row."" [Abu Dawud] ."
1094,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those on the right side of the rows” [Narrated by Abu Dawud with a chain of transmission according to the conditions of Muslim, and there is a man who differs in authenticating it.]."
1095,"And on the authority of Al-Baraa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: “When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we liked to be on his right, with his face facing us, so I heard him say: “My Lord, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect - or gather - Your servants.” [Muslim]."
1096,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Make the imam in the middle and close the gaps” [Abu Dawud]."
1097,"On the authority of the Mother of the Believers, Umm Habibah Ramla bint Abi Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with them both, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: There is no Muslim slave who prays to Allah Almighty every day twelve voluntary rak’ahs other than the obligatory one, except that Allah builds a house for him in Paradise, or: unless a house is built for him in Paradise” [Muslim]."
1098,"And on the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) two rak’ahs before noon and two rak’ahs after it, two rak’ahs after Friday, two rak’ahs after sunset, and two rak’ahs after the Isha prayer” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1099,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""There is a Salat (prayer) between every two Adhans; there is a Salat between every two Adhans."" (While saying the same for the) third time (he (ﷺ) added), ""It is for him who desires (to perform it)."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1100,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not miss four rak’ahs before noon, and two rak’ahs before dawn [Al-Bukhari]."
1101,"The Prophet (ﷺ) did not attach more importance to any Nawafil prayer than the two Rak'ah of prayer before dawn (Fajr) prayer. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1102,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""The two Rak'ah before the dawn (Fajr) prayer are better than this world and all it contains."" [Muslim] Another narration goes: ""The two Rak'ah before the dawn (Fajr) prayer are dearer to me than the whole world."""
1103,"I went to inform the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the time of the dawn (Fajr) prayer, and 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) kept me busy and began to ask me about something till the day grew bright. Then I got up and informed the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) of the time of Salat. I informed him again but he did not came out immediately to lead As- Salat. When he came out, he led As-Salat. I informed him that 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) had kept me busy with something she asked me about until the morning was almost full daylight, and that I had been delayed in coming to him. Upon that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""I was engaged in performing the two Rak'ahs of Fajr prayer."" Bilal (May Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Did the morning become very late (while you were praying)?"" He (ﷺ) replied, ""Even if the morning had become later than it did, I would have performed the two Rak'ahs and made them excellent and beautiful."" [Abu Dawud] ."
1104,"The Prophet (ﷺ) used to perform two Rak'ah short prayer between the Adhan (call to prayer) and the Iqamah of the dawn (Fajr) prayers. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] In another narration, 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform two supererogatory Rak'ah prayer of Fajr and make them so short in duration that I used to think whether he (ﷺ) had recited Surat Al-Fatihah (in it) or not. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] In the narration of Muslim, 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to hear the Adhan (of Fajr prayer) he would perform two supererogatory Rak'ah prayer and would make them short."
1105,"And on the authority of Hafsa, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when the muezzin called for dawn and dawn began, he would pray two light rak’ahs. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. And in a narration by Muslim: When dawn came, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would not pray except two light rak’ahs."
1106,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform his optional night prayers at night, two Rak'ah followed by two Rak'ah, and at the end he would conclude with an odd Rak'ah (Witr). Then he would perform two Rak'ahs prayer before the dawn (Fajr) prayer, and it was as if he could hear the Adhan being called due to his great alertness for the prayer time. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1107,"And on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to recite in the two rak’ahs of Fajr, in the first of them: {Say, “We believe in Allah and in what has been sent down to us,” the verse in Al-Baqarah, and in the second of them: “We believe in Allah, and bear witness that we are Muslims.” And in a narration: In the second (rak’ah), the verse from Al-Imran is: “Come to a common word between us and you.” [Muslim]."
1108,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited in the two dawn rak’ahs: {Say, O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, One} [Muslim]."
1109,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said that he observed the Prophet (ﷺ) for a month, while the Prophet (ﷺ) recited in the two rak’ahs before dawn: {Say, O disbelievers}, and: {Say: He is Allah, One}. [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1110,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed the two rak’ahs of Fajr, he would lie on his right side. [Al-Bukhari]."
1111,"When the Prophet (ﷺ) finished the 'Isha prayer, he would perform eleven Rak'ah before the Fajr prayer, concluding each two Rak'ah with Taslim (i.e., saying As-Salamu 'Alaikum) and observing the Witr (odd) at the end. When the Mu'adhdhin finished proclaiming Adhan for the Fajr prayer and it was dawn, he would rise and perform two short Rak'ah, and then would lie down on his right side till the Mu'adhdhin came to (inform) him about Iqamah. [Muslim] ."
1112,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you prays the two rak’ahs of Fajr, let him lie on his right.” ([Abu Dawud] Al-Tirmidhi said: It is a good and authentic hadith."
1113,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) two rak’ahs before noon, and two rak’ahs after it. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1114,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) did not miss four rak'ahs before noon. [Al-Bukhari]."
1115,"On her authority, she said: The Prophet (ﷺ) would pray four rak'ahs in my house before noon, then he would go out and lead the people in prayer, then he would enter and pray two rak’ahs, and he would pray the sunset prayer with the people, then he would enter my house and pray two rak’ahs, and he would lead the people in the evening prayer, and he would enter my house and pray two rak’ahs. [Muslim]."
1116,"On the authority of Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs four rak’ahs before noon and four after it, Allah will forbid him from Hell.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]. He said it is a good and authentic hadith."
1117,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray four rak'ahs after the sun had declined before the Zuhr prayer, and he said, “It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, and I would like for my good deeds to be performed during it.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1118,"If the Prophet (ﷺ) could not perform four Rak'ah before Zuhr prayer, he would perform them after it (i.e., after the obligatory prayer). [At-Tirmidhi] ."
1119,"On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that the Prophet (ﷺ) would pray four rak’ahs in the middle of the afternoon, separating them with greetings to the close angels and those who followed them among the Muslims and believers. It was narrated by Al-Tirmidhi and he said it was a good hadith."
1120,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""May Allah have mercy on a man who performs four Rak'ah before the 'Asr prayer."" [Abu Dawud and At- Tirmidhi] ."
1121,"On the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer. [Abu Dawud]."
1122,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Perform two Rak'ah before Maghrib prayer."" He (ﷺ) repeated it twice; when repeating it for the third time he added: ""He who may so wish."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
1123,"I saw the principal Companions of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) rushing to the pillars (of the mosque) to perform two Rak'ah prayers behind them before the Maghrib prayer. [Al-Bukhari] ."
1124,"On his authority, he said: During the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) we used to pray two rak’ahs after sunset and before Maghrib. It was said: Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pray them? He said: He used to see us praying them, but he did not command us nor forbid us. [Muslim]."
1125,"On his authority, he said: We were in Medina, and when the muezzin called for the Maghrib prayer, they would rush to the pillars and pray two rak'ahs, to the point that a strange man entering the mosque would think that the prayer had been prayed due to the large number of people praying. [Muslim]."
1126,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""If anyone of you performs the Friday prayer, he should perform four Rak'ah (Sunnah) after it."" [Muslim] ."
1127,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet (ﷺ) would not pray after Friday until he left, so he would pray two rak’ahs in his house. [Muslim]."
1128,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""O people! perform your (voluntary) Salat (prayers) in your homes because the best Salat of a man is the one he performs at home, except the obligatory Salat."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1129,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: Leave your prayers in your homes, and do not make them graves.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1130,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you performs his prayer in his mosque, let him give his house a share of his prayer, for Allah will make his prayer good in his house.” [Muslim]."
1131,"""Yes, I performed the Friday prayer along with him in the enclosure (Maqsurah), and when the Imam concluded the Salat with Taslim, I stood up in my place and performed the Sunnah prayer. When Mu'awiyah went home, he sent for me (and when I came) he said: ""Never do again what you have done. When you have observed the Friday prayer, you must not start another prayer till you have spoken to some one or have shifted your place; because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us not to follow up the congregational Salat with any other Salat until we have talked (to some one) or moved from the place."" [Muslim] ."
1132,"On the authority of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Witr prayer is not a seal like the obligatory prayer, but rather the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: “Allah is One (Witr) and loves the Witr prayer, so perform the Witr prayer, O people of the Qur’an.” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]. He said: A good hadith."
1133,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Throughout the night, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Witr prayer: at the beginning of the night, in the middle, and at the end. His Witr ended at the time of Suhur (pre-dawn). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1134,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Make Witr prayer the last of your Salat at night."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1135,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Perform Witr before the morning.” [Muslim]."
1136,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray at night, with her crossed in front of him, and when the Witr prayer remained, he woke her up and she performed the Witr prayer. [Muslim]. And in his narration: When the Witr prayer remained, he said: “Stand up and perform the Witr prayer, O Aisha.”"
1137,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Hasten to perform the Witr prayer before dawn."" [Abu Dawud and At-Tirmidhi] ."
1138,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever fears that he will not get up during the night, let him pray Witr at the beginning of the night, and whoever hopes to pray at the end of it, let him pray Witr at the end of the night, for the prayer at the end of the night is witnessed, and that is better.” [Muslim]."
1139,"My Khalil (the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)) directed me to fast three days of each month, and to observe two Rak'ah Duha (optional prayer) at forenoon, and to perform the Witr prayer before going to bed. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1140,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""In the morning, charity is due on every joint bone of the body of everyone of you. Every utterance of Allah's Glorification (i.e., saying Subhan Allah) is an act of charity, and every utterance of His Praise (i.e., saying Al-hamdu lillah) is an act of charity and every utterance of declaration of His Greatness (i.e., saying La ilaha illAllah) is an act of charity; and enjoining M'aruf (good) is an act of charity, and forbidding Munkar (evil) is an act of charity, and two Rak'ah Duha prayers which one performs in the forenoon is equal to all this (in reward)."" [Muslim] ."
1141,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray the Duha (forenoon) prayer four times, or more, as Allah wished. [Muslim]."
1142,"On the authority of Umm Hani’, his sister, daughter of Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: I went to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the year of the conquest, and I found him washing. When he finished washing, he prayed eight rak’ahs, and that was the Duha (forenoon) prayer. (Agreed upon, and this is a summary of the wording of one of Muslim’s narrations)"
1143,"On the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, that he saw people praying the Duha (forenoon) prayer, and he said: Did they not know that praying at other than this hour is better? The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The prayer of the penitent is when the young weaned camels tread on hot sand.” [Muslim]."
1144,"On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you enters the mosque, he should not sit until he has prayed two rak’ahs.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1145,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was in the mosque, and he said: “Pray two rak’ahs” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1146,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Bilal: O Bilal, tell me the most hopeful deed that you did in Islam, for I heard the drum of your sandals before me in Paradise. He said: I have not done a deed that is more hopeful to me than that I did not purify myself completely at any hour of the night or day without praying with that purification what was decreed for me to pray. ((Agreed upon, and this is the wording). Al-Bukhari).."
1147,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best day on which the sun rises is Friday: on it Adam was created, on it he was admitted to Paradise, and on it he was expelled from it.” [Muslim]."
1148,"On his authority, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then comes to the Friday prayer, and listens and listens, will be forgiven for what comes between that time and the Friday prayer, and an additional three days, and whoever touches pebbles has committed negligence” [Muslim]."
1149,"And on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The five daily prayers, Friday to Friday, and Ramadan to Ramadan, expiate what is between them if you avoid major sins” [Muslim]."
1150,"We heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying (while delivering Khutbah on his wooden pulpit), ""Either some people (i.e., hypocrites) stop neglecting the Friday prayers, or Allah will seal their hearts and they will be among the heedless."" [Muslim] ."
1151,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If one of you comes on Friday, let him perform ghusl (the full ritual bath)” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1152,"On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Ghusl on Friday is obligatory for everyone who has reached puberty” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1153,"On the authority of Samra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution on Friday will be blessed with it, and whoever performs ghusl, then ghusl is better” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
1154,"On the authority of Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “It is not obligatory for a man to perform ghusl on Friday, purify himself as much as he can, apply some of his own oil, or touch some of the perfume from his house, then go out, not separating between two people, then pray what is prescribed for him, then listen when the imam speaks, unless what comes between him and the next Friday is forgiven.” [Al-Bukhari].."
1155,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever performs ablution on a Friday ritual ritual ritual ritual ritual ritual bath, and then goes in the first hour, it is as if he had sacrificed a camel, and whoever departs in the second hour, it is as if he had sacrificed a cow, and whoever departed in the third hour, it is as if he had sacrificed a horned ram, and whoever departed in the fourth hour, it is as if he had sacrificed a chicken, and whoever departed in the fifth hour, it is as if he had sacrificed an egg, when the Imam emerges to lead the Friday prayer, the angels were present, listening to the remembrance” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1156,"On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned Friday, and said: “There is an hour in it when a Muslim servant, while standing and praying asking Allah for something, is present in that hour, Allah grants him his request,” and he gestured with his hand to shorten it, [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1157,"'Abdullah bin 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) said to me: ""Did you hear your father narrating something from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the special moment during Friday?"" I said: ""Yes, I heard him report from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): 'It occurs between the time when the Imam sits down (on the pulpit after the first Khutbah) and the time Salat is over.""' [Muslim] ."
1158,"On the authority of Aws bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “One of your best days is Friday, so send blessings upon me often, for your prayers are before me” [Abu Dawud]."
1159,"On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We left with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from Mecca, intending to go to Medina. When we were close to Azura, he descended, then raised his hands, and called upon Allah for an hour, then fell down in prostration, and stayed for a long time. Then he rose and raised his hands for an hour, then fell down in prostration - he did it - three times - and said: “I asked my Lord, and interceded for my nation, and He gave me a third of my nation, so I prostrated.” I prostrated to my Lord in thanks, then I raised my head and asked my Lord for my nation, and He gave me a third of my nation, so I fell down in prostration to my Lord in thanks. Then I raised my head and asked my Lord for my nation, and He gave me the other third, so I fell down in prostration to my Lord” [Abu Dawud]."
1160,"The Prophet (ﷺ) kept standing (in prayer) so long that the skin of his feet would crack. I asked him: ""Why do you do this, while you have been forgiven of your former and latter sins?"" He said, ""Should I not be a grateful slave of Allah?"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1161,"On the authority of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) knocked on the door of Ali and Fatima at night, and said: “Aren’t you praying?” (Agreed upon) (20)"
1162,"Salim bin 'Abdullah bin 'Umar bin Al-Khattab (May Allah be pleased with them) reported, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""What an excellent man 'Abdullah is! If only he could perform optional prayers at night."" Salim said that after this, (his father) 'Abdullah slept very little at night. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1163,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “O Abdullah, do not be like so-and-so: he used to pray the night prayers, but he abandoned the night prayers” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1164,"Mention was made before the Prophet (ﷺ) of a man who slept throughout the night till morning. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) remarked, ""He is a man in whose ears Satan urinated."" [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] .n"
1165,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Satan ties three knots on the head of one of you, when he sleeps, and strikes on each knot: ‘You have a long night, so sleep. If one of you wakes up and remembers Allah Almighty, one knot will be untied. If he performs ablution, one knot will be untied. If he prays, one knot will be untied, and he becomes energetic and has a good soul. Otherwise, he will become evil and lazy in soul.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1166,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “O people, spread peace, provide food, and pray at night while people are asleep, and you will enter Paradise in peace” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1167,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best fast after Ramadan is Allah’s month of Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory prayer is the night prayer.” [Muslim]."
1168,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Salat during the night should consist of pairs of rak'ahs; if you fear that morning is near, then pray one Rak'ah as Witr."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1169,"On his authority, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to pray at night two by two, and pray the Witr prayer with a rak’ah. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1170,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would break his fast during the month until we thought that he would not fast from it, and he would fast until we thought that he would not break his fast at all, and you would never look to see him praying at night without finding him praying, or look to see him sleeping without finding him sleeping. [Al-Bukhari]."
1171,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray eleven rak’ahs - meaning at night - prostrating as much as one of you recites fifty verses before raising his head, and he would pray two rak’ahs before the dawn prayer, then lie on his right side until the caller to prayer comes to him, [Al-Bukhari]."
1172,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not observe more than eleven Rak'ah (of Tahajjud prayers), be in Ramadan or any other month. First of all he would perform four Rak'ah. Ask not about their excellence and their length. He (ﷺ) would then perform four more Rak'ah; and do not ask about their excellence and their length. Then he would perform three Rak'ah (Witr prayer). ('Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) added) I submitted: ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you sleep before performing the Witr prayer?"" He (ﷺ) said, ""O 'Aishah! My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1173,"On her authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) used to sleep at the beginning of the night, and get up at the end of the night and pray. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1174,"On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) one night, and he remained standing until I thought about something bad. It was said: What did you think about? He said: I thought about sitting down and leaving him. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1175,"And on the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) one night, and he opened Al-Baqarah, and I said: He should bow at the hundred, then he went on, and I said: He should pray with it in a rak’ah, so he went on, and I said: He should kneel with it, then he opened with Al-Nisa’ and recited it, then he opened with Al-Imran, so he recited it, reciting slowly. If he came across a verse in which there is glorification, he glorified, and if he came across a verse containing a question, he would respond to it, and if he came across a verse of seeking refuge, he would seek refuge, then he bowed, and started saying: Glory be to my Lord the Great, so his bowing was similar to his standing, then he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, praise be to You. Then he stood for a long time, close to what he bowed, then he prostrated and said: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, so his prostration was close to his standing. [Muslim]."
1176,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: Which prayer is best? He said: “Long Qunoot” [Muslim]."
1177,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The most beloved prayer to Allah is the prayer of David, and the most beloved of fasting to Allah is the fasting of David. He used to sleep half the night, stand up for a third of it, sleep for a sixth of it, fast one day and break his fast the next.” (Agreed upon)"
1178,"On the authority of Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There is an hour in the night, during which if a Muslim man asks Allah Almighty for any good from the affairs of this world and the hereafter, He will give it to him, and that happens every night” [Muslim]."
1179,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""When one of you gets up at night to perform (Tahajjud) prayer, let him start Salat with two short Rak'ah."" [Muslim] ."
1180,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood for Salat at night, he would start his prayer with two brief Rak'ah. [Muslim] ."
1181,"If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) missed his night (Tahajjud) Salat because of indisposition or the like, he would perform twelve Rak'ah during the day. [Muslim] ."
1182,"On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever falls asleep from his portion (of the Qur'an), or from something of it, and recites it between the dawn prayer and the noon prayer, it will be recorded for him as if he had recited it during the night” [Muslim]."
1183,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “May Allah have mercy on a man who got up at night and prayed and woke up his wife, and if she refused, he sprinkled water on her face. May Allah have mercy on a woman who got up at night and prayed and woke up her husband, but if he refused, she sprinkled water on his face.” [Abu Dawud]."
1184,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When a man awakens his wife during the night and they both perform two Rak'ah Salat together, they are recorded among the men and women who celebrate remembrance of Allah."" [Abu Dawud] ."
1185,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “If one of you becomes sleepy during prayer, let him lie down until sleep goes away, for if one of you prays while he is sleepy, perhaps he will go and seek forgiveness and curse himself” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1186,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""When anyone of you stands up for Salat at night and finds it difficult to recite the Qur'an accurately and he is unaware of what he is reciting, he should go back to sleep."" [Muslim] ."
1187,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever prays Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1188,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to urge (the people) to perform (optional Tarawih) prayer at night during the month of Ramadan. He did not order them or make it obligatory on them. He (ﷺ) said, ""Whosoever performs (optional Tarawih) prayers at night during the month of Ramadan, with Faith and in the hope of receiving Allah's reward, will have his past sins forgiven."" [Muslim] ."
1189,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever prays Laylat al-Qadr out of faith and seeking reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1190,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that some of the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) saw the Night of Power in a dream during the last seven nights, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I see that your visions have coincided in the last seven nights, so whoever is searching for them, let him look for them in the last seven nights” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1191,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to seclude himself in the mosque during the last ten days of Ramadan, and say: “Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten days of Ramadan” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1192,"On her authority, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the odd-numbered nights of the last ten days of Ramadan” [Al-Bukhari]."
1193,"On her authority, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to: “When the last ten days of Ramadan began, he would live the night, wake up his family, exert himself in worship, and tighten his waist wrap” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1194,"On her authority, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to strive hard in Ramadan as he did not strive in any other time, and in the last ten days of it, he did what he did not strive in any other time” [Muslim]."
1195,"On her authority, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if I knew what Night of Destiny is, what would I say about it? He said: “Say: O Allah, You are the Pardoner and You love to pardon, so pardon me.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
1196,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Had I not thought it difficult for my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the Miswak (tooth-stick) before every Salat."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1197,"On the authority of Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) got up from sleep, he would use the siwak to clean his mouth. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1198,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: We used to prepare for the Messenger of Allah, his siwak and his purification, and Allah would awaken him as many times as He willed during the night, so he would use the siwak and wash his ablution and pray. [Muslim]."
1199,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I have increased your use of the siwak” [Al-Bukhari]."
1200,"On the authority of Shurayh bin Hani’, he said: I said to Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: What did the Prophet (ﷺ) start with when he entered his house? She said: With the siwak. [Muslim]."
1201,"On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and the tip of the siwak was on his tongue. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. This is the wording of Muslim."
1202,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""The Miswak (tooth-stick) cleanses and purifies the mouth and pleases the Rubb."" [An-Nasa'i and Ibn Khuzaimah] ."
1203,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “The fitrah is five, or five parts of the fitrah: circumcision, removing pubic hair, trimming the nails, plucking the armpits, and trimming the mustache” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] (24)"
1204,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Ten things are part of the fitrah: trimming the moustache, growing the beard, using the siwak, inhaling water, cutting the nails, washing the knuckles, plucking the armpits, shaving the pubic hair, and squeezing the water.” [The narrator said: And I forgot the tenth, unless it was rinsing the mouth. He said: Waki’ - and he is one of the Narrated by him-]. (25) [Muslim]. (( (26)"
1205,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Trim the moustaches and let the beard grow."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1206,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""(The structure of) Islam is built on five (pillars): Testification of 'La ilaha illallah' (none has the right to be worshipped but Allah), that Muhammad (ﷺ) is his slave and Messenger, the establishment of Salat, the payment of Zakat, the pilgrimage to the House of Allah (Ka'bah), and Saum during the month of Ramadan."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1207,"On the authority of Talha bin Ubaidullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) from the people of Najd, with disheveled hair. We could hear the echo of his voice, but we could not understand what he was saying. Until he approached the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he was asking about Islam. The Messenger (ﷺ) said: “Five prayers a day and a night.” He said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you volunteer.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “And fasting the month of Ramadan.” He said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned zakat to him, so he said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: “No, unless you do it voluntarily.” So the man turned around while he was saying: By Allah, I will neither add nor take away from this. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “He will succeed if he is truthful” (Agreed upon)."
1208,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent Mu’adh, may Allah be pleased with him, to Yemen and said: “Call them to testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. If they obey that, teach them that Allah Almighty has obligated five prayers on them every day and night. If they obey that, then teach them that Allah has obligated on them charity taken from their rich and given to their poor.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1209,"On the authority of Ibn Omar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I have been commanded to fight people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and perform prayer and pay zakat. If they do that, their blood and their wealth will be protected from me except for the right of Islam and their reckoning with Allah” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1210,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the Messenger of Allah died, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, declared disbelief among the Arabs who disbelieved, then Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: How can people be fought when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “I have been commanded to fight people until they say there is no god but Allah, so whoever says it, his wealth and his life are protected from me except by his right and his reckoning with Allah”?! So he said Abu Bakr: By Allah, I will fight anyone who differentiates between prayer and zakat, for zakat is the right of money. By Allah, if they prevented me from the headband that they used to give to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) I would fight them for withholding it. He said: Omar, may Allah be pleased with him: By Allah, it was only when I saw that Allah had opened Abu Bakr’s chest to fight, so I knew that it was the truth. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1211,"On the authority of Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said to the Prophet (ﷺ): Tell me about a deed that will take me into Paradise. He said: “You worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, and perform prayers, and pay zakat, and maintain family ties” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1212,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed that if I do it, I will enter Paradise. He said: “You worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, and perform prayers, and pay the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan.” He said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I will not do more than this.” When he turned to leave, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this one” (Agreed upon)."
1213,"On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I pledged allegiance to the Prophet (ﷺ) to establish prayer, pay zakat, and give sincere advice to every Muslim. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
1214,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Any person who possesses gold or silver and does not pay what is due on it (i.e., the Zakat); on the Day of Resurrection, sheets of silver and gold would be heated for him in the fire of Hell and with them his flank, forehead and back will be branded. When they cool down, they will be heated again and the same process will be repeated during the day the measure whereof will be fifty thousand years. (This would go on) until Judgement is pronounced among (Allah's) slaves, and he will be shown his final abode, either to Jannah or to Hell."" It was asked, ""How about someone who owns camels and does not pay what is due on him (i.e., their Zakat)?"" He (ﷺ) replied, ""In the same way the owner of camels who does not discharge what is due in respect of them (their due includes their milking on the day when they are taken to water) will be thrown prostrate on his face in a vast desert plain on the Day of Resurrection and they will trample upon him with their hoofs and bite him with their teeth. As often as the first of them passes him, the last of them will be made to return during a day the measure whereof will be fifty thousand years, until Judgement is pronounced among (Allah's) slaves, he will be shown his final abode either to Jannah or to Hell."" It was (again) asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what about cows (cattle) and sheep?"" He (ﷺ) said, ""If anyone who possesses cattle and sheep and does not pay what is due on them (i.e., their Zakat); on the Day of Resurrection, he will be thrown on his face in a vast plain desert. He will find none of the animals missing with twisted horns, without horns or with a broken horn, and they will gore him with their horns and trample upon him with their hoofs. As often as the first of them passes him, the last of them will be made to return to him during a day the measure whereof will be fifty thousand years, until Judgement is pronounced among (Allah's) slaves; and he will be shown his final abode either to Jannah or to Hell."" It was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what about the horses?"" Upon this he (ﷺ) said, ""The horses are of three types. One, which is a burden for the owner; another which is a shield, and another one which makes its owner entitled to reward. The one for whom these are a burden is the person who rears them for show or for pride or for causing injury to the sentiments of the Muslims. They will be a cause of torment for their owners. The one for whom these are a shield is the person who rears them for the sake of Allah but does not forget the Right of Allah concerning their backs and their necks (i.e., he lets a needy ride on them), and so they are a shield for him. Those which bring reward to the one who rears them in pastures and gardens are the ones that are used in the Cause of Allah (Jihad) by the Muslims. Whatever they eat from the meadows and the gardens will be recorded on his behalf as good deeds so much so that their droppings and urine will be counted for an equal number of good deeds for him. Even when they break their tying rope and every height from which they climb and every hoofprint which they leave will be counted as a good deed on behalf of the owner. When their owner leads them through a stream from which they drink, though he does not intend to quench their thirst, yet Allah would record for him the quantity (of water) of what they would drink on his behalf as good deeds."" It was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, what about the donkeys?"" Upon this he (ﷺ) said, ""Nothing has been revealed to me in regard to the donkeys in particular except this one Verse of a comprehensive nature: ""So whosoever does good equal to the weight of an atom (or a small ant) shall see it. And whosoever does evil equal to the weight of an atom (or a small ant) shall see it.""' (99: 8,9). [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1215,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Allah the Exalted and Majestic said: 'Every act of the son of Adam is for him, except As-Siyam (the fasting) which is (exclusively) for Me, and I will reward him for it.' Fasting is a shield. When anyone of you is observing fast, he should neither indulge in obscene language nor should he raise his voice; and if anyone reviles him or tries to quarrel with him, he should say: 'I am fasting.' By Him in Whose Hand the soul of Muhammad is, the breath of one observing Saum is sweeter to Allah than the fragrance of musk. The one who fasts, experiences two joys: he feels pleasure when he breaks the fast. He is joyful by virtue of his fast when he meets his Rubb."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] . In a narration by Al-Bukhari, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Allah says: '(The person observing Saum) has abstained from food and drink, and sexual pleasures for My sake; fasting is for Me, and I will bestow its reward. Every good deed has ten times its reward'."" In a narration by Muslim, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""The reward of every (good) deed of a person is multiplied from ten to seven hundred times. Allah (SWT) says: 'The reward of observing Saum is different from the reward of other good deeds; Saum is for Me, and I Alone will give its reward. The person observing Saum abstains from food and drink only for My sake.' The fasting person has two joyous occasions, one at the time of breaking his fast, and the other at the time of meeting his Rubb. Surely, the breath of one observing Saum is better smelling to Allah than the fragrance of musk."""
1216,"And on his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever spends two pairs for the sake of Allah, he will be called from the gates of Paradise: O servant of Allah, this is good. So whoever was among the people of prayer will be called from the gate of prayer, and whoever was among the people of jihad will be called from the gate of jihad, and whoever was among the people of fasting will be called from the gate of ar-Rayyan, and whoever was among the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity.” Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. O Messenger of Allah, there is no hardship on the one who is called from these gates. Is anyone called from all of these gates? He said: “Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them” (Agreed upon)"
1217,"On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “In Paradise there is a gate called: Al-Rayyan, through which those who are fasting will enter on the Day of Resurrection and no one else will enter through it. It will be said: Where are those who are fasting? They will stand up, and no one else will enter through it. Then when they enter, it will be closed and no one else will enter through it. They will stand up, and no one else will enter through it. Then when they enter, it will be closed and no one else will enter through it."
1218,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Every slave of Allah who observes Saum (fasting) for one day for the sake of Allah, Allah will draw his face farther from Hell-fire to the extent of a distance to be covered in seventy years."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1219,"The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""He who observes fasting during the month of Ramadan with Faith while seeking its reward from Allah, will have his past sins forgiven."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1220,"And on his authority, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained up” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1221,"On his authority, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it, and if it (the moon) is obscured from you, then complete the number of days of Sha’ban as thirty days” [Agreed upon, and this is the wording of Al-Bukhari]. And in Muslim’s narration: “And if it is cloudy for you, then fast thirty days.”"
1222,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the most generous of the men; and he was the most generous during the month of Ramadan when Jibril visited him every night and recited the Qur'an to him. During this period, the generosity of Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) waxed faster than the rain bearing wind. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1223,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When the last ten days (of Ramadan) entered, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would liven up the night, wake up his family, and tighten his waist wrapper. (Agreed upon)"
1224,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “None of you should precede Ramadan by fasting a day or two, unless he is a man who used to fast during his fast, then let him fast that day.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1225,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it. If it (the moon) is obscured from you, then complete thirty days.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
1226,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If half of Shaban remains, do not fast” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1227,"On the authority of Abu Al-Yaqzan Ammar bin Yasser, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: “Whoever fasts on the day of which he has doubts has disobeyed Abu Al-Qasim (ﷺ)” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
1228,"At the sight of the new moon (of the lunar month), the Prophet (ﷺ) used to supplicate: ""Allahumma ahillahu 'alaina bil-amni wal-iman, was-salamati wal-Islam, Rabbi wa Rabbuk-Allah, Hilalu rushdin wa khairin (O Allah, let this moon appear on us with security and Iman; with safety and Islam. (O moon!) Your Rubb and mine is Allah. May this moon be bringing guidance and good)."" [At- Tirmidhi] ."
1229,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Eat Suhur (predawn meal). Surely, there is a blessing in Suhur."" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1230,"On the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We had suhoor with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then we stood up for prayer. It was said, “How much was there between them?” He said: Fifty verses [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1231,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had two Mu'adhdhin: Bilal and Ibn Umm Maktum (May Allah be pleased with them). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""Bilal proclaims Adhan [call to Salat (prayer)] at fag end of night, so eat and drink till Ibn Umm Maktum pronounces Adhan."" Ibn 'Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) added: And the gap between their Adhan was not more than the time spent in one's getting down and the other's climbing (the minaret). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1232,"On the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah said: “The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is that we eat the pre-dawn meal (suhoor), which they do not. [Muslim]."
1233,"On the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “People will continue to be well as long as they hasten to break the fast.” (Agreed upon)"
1234,"Masruq and I visited 'Aishah (May Allah be pleased with her) and said: ""O Mother of the Believers! There are two Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ) and neither of them holds back from doing good acts; but one of them hastens to break Saum (fasting) and hastens to perform the Maghrib prayer, while the other delays breaking Saum and delays performing Salat (prayer)."" She asked, ""Who is the one who hastens to break Saum and perform the Maghrib prayer?"" Masruq said, ""It is 'Abdullah (meaning 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud)."" She said, ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do so."" [Muslim] ."
1235,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Allah Almighty said: “The most beloved of My servants to me are those who are quickest to break the fast” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1236,"On the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “When the night approaches from here and the day departs from here, and the sun sets, then the fasting person has broken his fast” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1237,"On the authority of Abu Ibrahim Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: We walked with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was fasting. When the sun set, he said to some of the people: “O so-and-so, come down and do good for us.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, what if it were evening?” He said: “Come down and do good for us.” He said: “You have a day.” He said: “Come down and grind (dates) for us.” He said: So he came down and ground dates for them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drank and then said: “If you see night approaching from here, then the fasting person has broken his fast,” and he pointed with his hand towards the east. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1238,"I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, ""When one of you breaks his Saum (fasting), let him break it on dates; if he does not have any, break his fast with water for it is pure."" [Abu Dawud] ."
1239,"On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would break his fast before praying with fresh dates, and if there were not fresh dates, then dates, and if there were not dates, then a sip of water. [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
1240,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If it is a day for one of you to fast, he should not be obscene or make noise. If anyone insults him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting.”"
1241,"On his authority, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever does not give up false speech and acting upon it, Allah has no need for him to give up his food and drink” [Al-Bukhari]."
1242,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If one of you forgets and eats or drinks, let him complete his fast, for Allah has only fed him and given him drink.” (Agreed upon)"
1243,"On the authority of Laqit bin Sabra, may Allah be pleased with him, he said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, tell me about ablution? He said, “Perform ablution thoroughly, between the fingers, and inhale deeply, unless you are fasting” [Abu Dawud and Al-Tirmidhi]."
1244,"On the authority of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to be overtaken by dawn while he was in a state of janabah from his family, then he would perform ghusl and fast [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1245,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would wake during Ramadan (fasting) in a state of major impurity without a wet dream, but on account of sexual intercourse and he would take a bath before dawn. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1246,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “The best fast after Ramadan is the month of Allah, Muharram, and the best prayer after the obligatory prayer is the night prayer” [Muslim]."
1247,"The Prophet (ﷺ) did not observe voluntary Saum (fasting) so frequently during any other month as he did during Sha'ban. He observed Saum throughout the month of Sha'ban. Another narration is: He (ﷺ) observed Saum during the whole month of Sha'ban except a few days. [Al- Bukhari and Muslim] ."
1248,"And on the authority of Mujibah Al-Bahiliyya, on the authority of her father or uncle, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then he set off and came to him after a year, and his condition and appearance had changed, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not know me? He said: “And who are you?” He said: I am the Bahili who came to you in the first year. He said: “So what changed you, since you were of good appearance?” He said: “I have not eaten food since I left you except at night.” Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “You tortured yourself!” Then he said: “Fast for the month of patience, and one day every month.” He said: “Add me, for there is strength in me.” He said: “Fast for two days.” He said: “Increase for me.” He said: “Fast for three days.” He said: “Add me.” He said: “Fast one day and leave one day, fast one day and leave one day, fast one day and leave one day.” He said with his three fingers and joined them together, then released them. [Narrated by Abu Dawud.]."
1249,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, ""There are no days during which the righteous action is so pleasing to Allah than these days (i.e., the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah)."" He was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, not even Jihad in the Cause of Allah?"" He (ﷺ) replied, ""Not even Jihad in the Cause of Allah, except in case one goes forth with his life and his property and does not return with either of it."" [Al- Bukhari] ."
1250,"On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: About fasting on the day of Arafat? He said: “It expiates the past year and the coming year” [Muslim]."
1251,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) fasted on the day of Ashura, and ordered that it be fasted. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1252,"On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about fasting on the day of Ashura, and he said: “It expiates the previous year” [narrated by Muslim]."
1253,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If I stay until the next year, I will fast on the ninth” [Muslim]."
1254,"On the authority of Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six days of Shawwal, it will be like fasting for a lifetime” [Muslim]."
1255,"On the authority of Abu Qatada, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about fasting on Monday, and he said: “That is the day on which I was born, and the day on which I was sent or revealed to me” [Muslim]."
1256,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) he said: “Deeds are presented on Mondays and Thursdays, so I would like for my deeds to be presented while I am fasting” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1257,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to observe fast on Mondays and Thursdays. [At-Tirmidhi] ."
1258,"On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My friend (ﷺ) advised me to do three things: fasting three days of every month, praying the two rak’ahs of the forenoon prayer, and praying Witr before I sleep. [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1259,"On the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: My beloved (ﷺ) advised me to do three things that I will never abandon as long as I live: to fast three days of every month, to pray the forenoon prayer, and not to sleep until I have prayed Witr. [Muslim]."
1260,"On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: “Fasting three days of every month is fasting for an entire lifetime” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
1261,"Mu'adhah al-Adawiyyah (May Allah be pleased with her) asked 'Aishah Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) use to observe three days of Saum (fasting) in every month?"" She replied, ""Yes."" I asked, ""On which days in the month did he observed fast?"" She replied that he did not mind on which days of the month he observed fast. [Muslim] ."
1262,"On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If you fast three days of the month, then fast thirteen, fourteen and fifteen.” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
1263,"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) directed us to observe Saum (fasting) on the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth of the (lunar) month. [Abu Dawud] ."
1264,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) “would not break his fast during the white days while he was at home or traveling” [Narrated by Al-Nasa’i with a good chain of transmission]."
1265,"On the authority of Zaid bin Khaled Al-Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) who said: “Whoever provides food for a fasting person to break their fast will have a reward similar to his reward, except that nothing will be diminished from the reward of the fasting person” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
1266,"Once the Prophet (ﷺ) visited us and I served him some food. He (ﷺ) asked me to eat. I replied that I was observing (optional) fast. He (ﷺ) said, ""When people eat by a person observing fast, the angels continually send blessings upon that person until they have had their fill."" [At-Tirmidhi] ."
1267,"The Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit Sa'd bin 'Ubadah (May Allah be pleased with him) who presented bread and olive oil to him. The Prophet (ﷺ) ate it and said, ""The observers of fast have broken their fast with you (this is the literal translation, but the meaning is: 'May Allah reward you for providing a fasting people with food to break their fast'); the pious people have eat your food and the angels invoked blessings on you."" [Abu Dawud] ."
